Our client, the number one credit insurer in the world, is searching for an AWS DevOps Engineer/Cloud Engineer to join the team in charge of the design, standardization, and implementation of the infrastructure, the CI/CD pipeline, and the monitoring stack of their system.
 Job Responsibilities: 
 • Ia-C & Infrastructure Architecture – Design and build reusable, secure, and auditable Ia-C modules using Terraform, Terragrunt, and AWS CDK;
 • CI/CD & Delivery – Implement, maintain, and continuously improve automated CI/CD pipelines (GitLab/GitHub) for testing and deployment; review submitted merge requests;
 • Observability & Operations – Ensure full system visibility by implementing monitoring, logging, and alert management (Grafana, Prometheus, Dynatrace, PagerDuty); participate in regular on call duty to ensure production stability;
 • Security & FinOps – Implement security frameworks (policy-as-code) and optimize AWS cloud spend using FinOps practices (Cost Explorer, Compute Optimizer);
 • Collaboration & Agile Execution – Work closely with squad members, Product Owners, and transversal IT teams in an Agile environment (SAF e, Scrum).
 Job Requirements: 
 • Strong hands-on experience with AWS managed services and event-driven architectures (e.g., DynamoDB, Lambdas, Kinesis, Fargate, EMR, Aurora, PostgreSQL, MySQL, OpenSearch/Elasticsearch);
 • Solid understanding of monitoring and alerting stacks (Grafana, Prometheus, Prometheus Alertmanager, Dynatrace, PagerDuty);
 • Familiarity with FinOps tooling and cost management (AWS Cost Explorer, Compute Optimizer) is a strong plus;
 • Familiarity with Agile methods and frameworks (SAF e, Scrum);
 • Working knowledge of French is a plus (English or French used as working languages in squads).
 Required Qualifications: 
 • Deep hands-on expertise with AWS Cloud following Well-Architected practices;
 • Full proficiency in Infrastructure as Code (Ia C) using Terraform, Terragrunt, and AWS CDK;
 • Strong background in CI/CD pipeline implementation and version control using GitLab and GitHub;
 • Proficient with both Linux and Windows operating systems;
 • Fluency in English (mandatory for all documentation and project communications.
 Personal Characteristics: 
 • Structured and analytical mindset with strong problem-solving capabilities;
 • Excellent communication, interpersonal, and team-player skills;
 • Ability to work autonomously while aligning closely with transversal teams and stakeholders.
